Sticky Position: Ensure the Navbar is sticky or fixed at the top of the screen so users can navigate easily while scrolling through long content sections.

B. Portfolio

Focus: Reusable ProjectCard Component. This is your most valuable section.

Essential Work:

Data Source: Define your projects using a static JSON array in a separate data file (or directly in your component file). This makes maintenance easy.

ProjectCard Props: Create a single, reusable component (ProjectCard) that accepts props for: Title, Description, Technologies Used, Image/Screenshot URL, GitHub Link, and Live Demo Link.

Grid Layout: Use a responsive CSS Grid (or Tailwind CSS grid classes) to display the cards cleanly on desktop (e.g., 2 or 3 columns) and stack them on mobile.

Alternative: For simplicity, provide a direct mailto: link on a prominent "Send Email" button.

By focusing on these specific content and functional requirements for each component, you will ensure your portfolio is professional, highly readable, and effective at showcasing your skills.

